{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-two-row-projection","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:two-row-projection","kind":"definition","title":"Two-row projection $\\pi_{\\mathrm{2-row}}$ onto the two-row Wedderburn subalgebra","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-two-row-stratum","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-wedderburn-weight-canonical"],"tags":["wedderburn-decomposition","su2-schur-weyl","two-row","projection"],"defines":["two-row-projection"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRowStratum.HasTwoRowProjection","text":"two-row-projection.md","leanSource":"two-row-projection.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:two-row-projection\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda^2(n)</code> be the <a href=\"#def:two-row-stratum\" data-at=\"mass-theory/hoefsmit-convergence-magic-shells/hoefsmit-he4-magic-a-binding\">two-row stratum</a> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(q)</code>. The <dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-two-row-projection\">two-row projection</dfn> is the orthogonal projection onto the two-row Wedderburn subalgebra:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\pi_{\\mathrm{2-row}} \\;\\colon\\; H_n(q) \\;\\to\\;\n    \\bigoplus_{\\lambda \\in \\Lambda^2(n)} \\mathrm{End}(V_\\lambda).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/two-row-projection.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.7.2","page":"b/def-two-row-projection","qa":{"counts":{"pass":52,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":63}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:BraidKnotOctonion.TwoRowStratum.HasTwoRowProjection","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/two-row-projection.lean","compiles":"unc